<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nagasaki</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nagasaki is a port city on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a> it was the only permitted point of contact with European traders, through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> post at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dejima">Dejima</a>, and a centre of controlled Chinese trade. On 9 August 1945 it was struck by an atomic bomb, an event that helped bring about the surrender of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nagasaki.jpg" alt="Nagasaki" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tomio344456 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nagasaki_City_View_from_Glover_Garden,_Nagasaki_2014.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
